  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize uncovering the face-down cards in the rightndmost columns, as they contain the largest stacks of hidden cards.\n\nEmpty slots: If you don't have a King to move, do not empty a column. You lose a vital building spot that could be used for lower-rank cards.\n\nLook deep into the stacks. Since any group can move, you can often pull a needed 5 from the middle of a messy stack to move it to a 6 elsewhere, provided the 5 is face-up.",
    Player: "Prioritize uncovering the face-down cards in the rightndmost columns, as they contain the largest stacks of hidden cards.\n\nEmpty slots: If you don't have a King to move, do not empty a column. You lose a vital building spot that could be used for lower-rank cards.\n\nLook deep into the stacks. Since any group can move, you can often pull a needed 5 from the middle of a messy stack to move it to a 6 elsewhere, provided the 5 is face-up.",
